|=0?$\n\nI. $A$ has proportional rows\n\nII. $A$ has proportional columns\n\nIII. $A$ has identical rows" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186572686 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "3e928130-63ab-538e-924b-5fd72d363a24" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186572686 #edb/ref 1074 "Let's examine each of the statements in turn.\n\n- $A$ has proportional rows: \n\n$$\nA=\\begin{bmatrix}5 & 1 & -1 \\\\ 2 & 0 & 1 \\\\ 10 & 2 & -2\\end{bmatrix}\\,✓\n$$\n\n- $A$ does *not* have proportional columns.\n\n- $A$ does *not* have identical rows.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I only.\"" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186572700 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186572593 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186572700 #edb/ref 1069 "q-42470" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186572700 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186572700 #edb/ref 1071 "Find $6det(A)-2det(B)$, where \n\n$$\nA=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 7 & 3 & 2 \\\\ \\sqrt{3} & 1 & 2 & 9 \\\\ 1 & 7 & 3 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 5\\end{bmatrix},\\,B=\\begin{bmatrix}3\\sqrt{2} & 3 \\\\ 1 & 0\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186572700 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "7fe1aa9d-37dc-5179-a9aa-2b200892c342" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186572700 #edb/ref 1074 "Let's examine each matrix in turn.\n\n- Since $A$ has two identical rows, we obtain\n\n$$\nA=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 7 & 3 & 2 \\\\ \\sqrt{3} & 1 & 2 & 9 \\\\ 1 & 7 & 3 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 5\\end{bmatrix}\\,⟹\\,det(A)=0.\n$$\n\n- Since $B$ is a $2\\times 2$ matrix, its determinant is:\n\n$$\ndet(B)=3\\sqrt{2}\\cdot 0-1\\cdot 3=-3\n$$\n\nTherefore, $6det(A)-2det(B)=6\\cdot 0-2\\cdot (-3)=6.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417]}
